# L1: the AUDITED smoke of prompt-lookup drafting on c2-packed-tp4-best-lookup (c2-packed-tp4-best-strace plus QWEN_FAST_LOOKUP_DRAFT=n3m12, nothing else). The FIRST four-card job of the window,
# so its actions put rescan before the reset: a board that dropped off the bus without a by-id link is recovered before the quad is reset.
# THE ARM DEPENDS ON IT: a failure here means TL1 to TL4 are skipped by the driver; the window itself continues.
# READ: one '[LOOKUP-DRAFT] engaged policy=n3m12' line per request and one '[LOOKUP-ROUND]' line per user per round (source=lookup or dflash2, proposed 0..15, committed 1..16); c2_smoke_check clean
# (its lookup rule: an engaged line naming the policy, round lines well formed); the texts of concurrent4_code_equal EQUAL the control arm's (TL1's hashes): the lookup only changes which tokens are
# verified, the verifier's greedy argmax decides every token, so a different text is a bug, not noise. No stall. Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min, engine build 10-30 min, the smoke 30-60 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/lookup four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/lookup and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lookup-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/lookup commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=rescan reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lookup-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-lookup
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,concurrent4_code_equal
